// Generic campaign outros — used when no archetype is active.
// Variables set before running: $player_faction, $enemy_faction, $sector_name,
//   $missions_won, $total_missions, $date

title: outro_generic_win
---
Narrator: {$date}
Narrator: The sector is called {$sector_name}. It is yours.

Narrator: Final status: {$player_faction} has achieved decisive victory over {$enemy_faction} within {$sector_name}. Enemy command structure dismantled. Remaining opposition eliminated, scattered, or withdrawn beyond operational reach.

The war is over. The war is over. The war is over. 

The war is over. And your mind is still fighting it.
-> New Campaign
    <<narrative_action "new_campaign">>
-> Random Missions
    <<narrative_action "random_missions">>
-> Quit
    <<narrative_action "quit">>
===

title: outro_generic_loss
---
Narrator: Commander,

The campaign is over. {$player_faction} secured {$missions_won} of {$total_missions} engagements — and it was not enough.
Narrator: {$enemy_faction} held their ground with a steadiness we could not match. The sector remains beyond our reach. Our council will want an accounting of how it came to this: how kinsmen who share our tongue and our traditions proved the stronger hand.

We are no longer favoured by the stars. That is a harder defeat than any single lost engagement.

For now — it ends here.
-> New Campaign
    <<narrative_action "new_campaign">>
-> Random Missions
    <<narrative_action "random_missions">>
-> Quit
    <<narrative_action "quit">>
===
